                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc1e3e37-ae5f-4c6f-b9d4-d6831f3e1872",
                                                "sense_id": "9a752f43-3e5e-3dda-a8a7-3948789a68aa",
                                                "text": "“There the cause of death was soon ascertained ; the victim of this daring outrage had been stabbed to death from ear to ear with a long, sharp instrument, in shape like an antique stiletto, which […] was subsequently found under the cushions of the hansom.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cd5727a-5b9a-4584-b362-fab5b21525f5",
                                                "sense_id": "9a752f43-3e5e-3dda-a8a7-3948789a68aa",
                                                "text": "There were many wooden chairs for the bulk of his visitors, and two wicker armchairs with red cloth cushions for superior people. From the packing-cases had emerged some Indian clubs,[…], and all these articles[…] made a scattered and untidy decoration that Mrs. Clough assiduously dusted and greatly cherished."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e8eaf96-46af-3af6-9e42-95960d7c855a",
